{
  "title": "skyBlip diagnostics record layout (v1)",
  "description": "The one place the diagnostics record layout is written. scripts/diagnostics_layout.py generates from it the firmware's type codes, payload offsets, flag bits and enum codes (firmware/core/diagnostics/layout.h), the test that pins each mirrored C++ enum to its codes (firmware/test/core/diagnostics/test_diagnostics_mirrors.cpp), and the decoder tables of scripts/blip_records.py and server/app/javascript/skyblip/diagnostics.js. scripts/check_diagnostics_layout.py fails when a generated file differs from what the generator writes, and holds schemas/diagnostics_log.v1.schema.json, the decoded view, to the names here. A record is 24 bytes: type, flags, into_ms, at_s and a 16-byte payload, which a field's at counts from. Flag bits 0 and 1 belong to the envelope, so a type's own flags take bits 2 to 7. A field's kind is one of u8, i8, u16, i16, u24, u32 and i32, read little-endian; enum8, a byte decoded through the named enum, where a code the enum does not hold decodes as its number; code8, a byte holding the named enum's code, decoded as the number; bits, width bits of one byte from bit shift up; flag, a flag bit decoded as a boolean; and vouch, a flag bit read only to vouch for another field. scale multiplies the decoded number. valid_when names a flag of the same type: the field is left out when that flag reads false, and kept when the flag is itself left out. A retired field is decoded from older captures and never written, and nothing reuses its bytes or bits. The decoders write a type's fields in the order listed. A type code and an enum code are never renumbered, because a capture outlives the firmware that wrote it, so a new type or member takes the next free code. An enum is declared by layout.h, mirrors a C++ enum member by member, or names the codes of a product's own enum, which the product's tests pin.",
